  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-HOLDER-RESOLVED-COMPONENT-ID-001",
      "severity": "P2 provisional; conditional panic in a public construction path, no runtime result",
      "classification": "same first-failure family as checkpoint 059 holder original optional ID, independently traced at 95e",
      "detail": "Recipe Component.id is optional; resolved_id chooses the explicit ID, then label, then an indexed generated name. Recipe validation checks the resolved ID and holder_identity checks source role or shape, but does not require an explicit original ID. Construction resolves a private recipe clone and writes each resolved ID there. After construction, HolderConstruction selects the original fitted component and expects its original id for a sheath blade or a haft-loop grip. If an otherwise valid fitted recipe with a selected absent ID passes construction, this expectation panics before a recoverable holder result is returned.",
      "source_case": "The checked-in longsword has a lofted blade with id and label both \"blade\". As a source-derived conditional case, replacing only that id with None leaves the effective identity \"blade\" and leaves referenced frame names unchanged; the checked-in source itself still has the ID. If that modified recipe otherwise passes the actual construction, the default sheath selects this original component and its expect panics. This is not a generated fixture, proof of construction success, a test, or an observed panic.",
      "boundary": "Public generate_holder, validate_holder, derive_holder_properties, holder codec encode/decode and EvaluatedHolder eventually use the constructor. The browser request dispatcher exposes GenerateHolder to the library boundary. Strategic smithing decodes submitted weapon recipes and can persist a valid evaluated weapon; separately, generated loadout provisioning fits a holder. No connected source establishes that an ordinarily forged weapon is later fitted by that provisioning path, that a client submitted this case, or that any deployment exposes it.",
      "safeguards": "Recipe validation enforces real identity, structural, manufacturing and construction checks; holder validation enforces kind and parameter constraints. Preserve legal label and generated identity modes and existing malformed geometry errors rather than requiring all authored IDs. The authored default catalog has an explicit blade ID; do not claim it is broken.",
      "connected_scope": "Recipe effective ID and frame references, resolved construction/source mapping, sheath and haft-loop selection, holder validation/evaluation/codecs and browser/strategic consumers, existing error classifications and all aliases.",
      "proposed_repair": "After audit completion, make holder source selection use the same admitted effective component identity or resolved selected source used by construction; retain supported absent-ID authoring and genuine missing-geometry errors.",
      "later_acceptance": "When product validation is authorized, cover explicit IDs, matching-label effective IDs and generated identities for sheath and haft-loop sources, frame references and invalid/missing geometry across direct evaluation, codec and supported consumers; verify no panic and preserve valid existing results.",
      "historical_related_candidates": [
        "SEGOVB-L12-HOLDER-ORIGINAL-OPTIONAL-ID-EXPECT",
        "PL13-HOLDER-OPTIONAL-COMPONENT-ID"
      ],
